1
00:00:00,042 --> 00:00:02,264
Dad, this is Mr. Guero.

2
00:00:02,298 --> 00:00:06,001
Hey, Guero, how're you doing?
This is my father.

3
00:00:06,035 --> 00:00:08,177
Mariano, serve them well.

4
00:00:08,211 --> 00:00:12,400
-He's nice. I like him already.
-He's great, you'll see.

5
00:00:12,434 --> 00:00:14,992
What will it be, chief?
And for you, princess?

6
00:00:15,026 --> 00:00:16,776
"Princess." Did you hear it?

7
00:00:16,810 --> 00:00:19,437
Same as always:
the ranch, Guero.

8
00:00:19,471 --> 00:00:22,786
Mariano, a ranch
with double guacamole and tortilla.

9
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:25,675
Easy, I still want to fit
in my dress.

10
00:00:25,709 --> 00:00:28,051
-And you, chief?
-Don't call me "chief".

11
00:00:28,085 --> 00:00:31,319
I'm Jaime.
Come here, give me a hug.

12
00:00:31,353 --> 00:00:33,168
-That's great!
-Jaime.

13
00:00:33,202 --> 00:00:34,984
-Is the truck yours?
-Yes.

14
00:00:35,018 --> 00:00:37,278
I'm the owner here.
Right, Mariano?

15
00:00:37,312 --> 00:00:39,216
-Yes.
-Wow, it's so delicious, Dad!

16
00:00:39,250 --> 00:00:41,551
They're the best
in the neighborhood.

17
00:00:41,585 --> 00:00:44,821
-You can trust him.
-Yes, only the best ingredients.

18
00:00:44,855 --> 00:00:48,657
-Only prime steak, chief.
-And prime napkins,

19
00:00:48,691 --> 00:00:51,225
prime cheese, bacon
and sausages too.

20
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:53,961
-His sausage is amazing!
-I didn't see that coming.

21
00:00:53,995 --> 00:00:56,782
I really admire self-made men.

22
00:00:56,816 --> 00:01:00,912
My daughter told me that
tacos al pastor are your specialty.

23
00:01:00,946 --> 00:01:05,043
Try some, please.
Give it to that young lady.

24
00:01:07,928 --> 00:01:12,545
What the hell? Who's this?
You were all over her.

25
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:14,172
-Who's she?
-I beg your pardon?

26
00:01:14,206 --> 00:01:16,365
-Who's she?
-Remember, young man:

27
00:01:16,399 --> 00:01:18,614
if you're not honest,
you just sell tacos.

28
00:01:18,648 --> 00:01:20,906
Wait, it's okay.

29
00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:23,475
This lady is an old customer.
Right, Mari?

30
00:01:23,509 --> 00:01:25,586
Since we had a tiny tent.

31
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:28,888
-It looked like a toy.
-A small table and she was here.

32
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,706
-Well, this changes everything.
-Sure.

33
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:35,382
-I'm sorry. Enjoy your meal.
-We're really sorry.

34
00:01:35,416 --> 00:01:38,151
-You're my only hope, you know?
-Me? Why is that?

35
00:01:38,185 --> 00:01:42,305
I'd given up on her.
She's 30 and still lives with me.

36
00:01:42,339 --> 00:01:44,352
She didn't go to college.
It's okay.

37
00:01:44,386 --> 00:01:48,057
She thinks she's a coach
for make-up made of leftovers.

38
00:01:48,091 --> 00:01:50,864
She says she sells hot pictures
on OnlyFans,

39
00:01:50,898 --> 00:01:54,131
but she didn't sell any picture.
Not a single one!

40
00:01:54,165 --> 00:01:56,322
I was thrilled when she told me

41
00:01:56,356 --> 00:01:59,126
-she wanted me to meet some guy.
-That's right.

42
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:00,307
Of course.

43
00:02:00,341 --> 00:02:03,648
I see that you two
have something special.

44
00:02:03,682 --> 00:02:07,857
-I think you're confused, chief.
-No, I'm happy

45
00:02:07,891 --> 00:02:10,606
to think about the grandchildren
you'll give me.

46
00:02:10,640 --> 00:02:12,831
The first one will be Joel,
after grandpa.

47
00:02:12,865 --> 00:02:14,119
What Joel?

48
00:02:14,153 --> 00:02:17,171
No! If I had a boy,
I'd name him Jorge.

49
00:02:17,205 --> 00:02:20,260
Not Joel, or Bryan, or Guero Jr!

50
00:02:20,294 --> 00:02:24,310
I have nothing with your daughter.
I sell tacos, that's my job.

51
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:27,926
What do you mean?
What is your Guero saying?

52
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:31,712
Your Guero, our Guero,
their Guero my ass!

53
00:02:32,595 --> 00:02:35,277
There's a piece to everyone.
Accept it!

54
00:02:35,311 --> 00:02:39,397
Dad, Guero cooks for me
and calls me "princess".

55
00:02:39,431 --> 00:02:42,618
I don't even need to do the dishes.
What man does that?

56
00:02:42,652 --> 00:02:44,836
-You're right.
-Good afternoon.

57
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:47,038
Hi, good afternoon.

58
00:02:47,072 --> 00:02:48,744
-Excuse me.
-Go ahead.

59
00:02:48,778 --> 00:02:51,350
-Just a second, mama.
-"Mama"? Mr. Guero.

60
00:02:51,384 --> 00:02:53,953
why didn't you tell me
your mom was so pretty?

61
00:02:53,987 --> 00:02:55,319
It's ready.

62
00:03:03,263 --> 00:03:06,766
Hi, Mariano. Where's Mr. Guero?

63
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,248
He won't be here today, blondie.

64
00:03:09,282 --> 00:03:12,881
-He's buying meat.
-Oh, really?

65
00:03:13,808 --> 00:03:16,864
-Is everything okay?
-He didn't tell me anything.

66
00:03:16,898 --> 00:03:20,425
But I'm here.
What will it be, blondie?

67
00:03:20,697 --> 00:03:23,084
I'd like a suadero, but...

68
00:03:23,118 --> 00:03:26,315
No!
I can't do this to Mr. Guero.

69
00:03:26,349 --> 00:03:29,462
Why not, blondie?
A taco suadero, right away.

70
00:03:29,496 --> 00:03:31,947
Well, I'll have a ranch too.

71
00:03:31,981 --> 00:03:34,916
-Okay. Would like some fries?
-It's your call.

72
00:03:35,387 --> 00:03:38,419
-Hum, yummy...
-Andrea.

73
00:03:38,453 --> 00:03:40,776
No, Mr. Guero,
it's not what you're thinking.

74
00:03:40,810 --> 00:03:44,331
-No, I would never do that to you.
-Mariano,

75
00:03:44,365 --> 00:03:46,593
when did I bit your taco?

76
00:03:46,627 --> 00:03:49,988
But... tacos are meant to share.

77
00:03:51,195 --> 00:03:53,775
Each one
with their own meat, okay?